=== One-offs ===
[[File:Usain Bolt Nissan GT-R (8403076829) (cropped).jpg|alt=|thumb|GT-R Bolt Edition displayed at the 2013 North American International Auto Show]]
Various one-off editions were built throughout the years. In 2012, "Usain Bolt" one-off GT-R, named after the athlete [[Usain Bolt]], was built and auctioned off to raise funds for charity. A display model was held in Tokyo, Japan.<ref>{{Cite web|title=Aussie buys gold Usain Bolt Nissan GT-R|url=https://www.carsales.com.au/editorial/details/aussie-buys-gold-usain-bolt-nissan-gt-r-34150/|access-date=2020-06-27|website=www.carsales.com.au}}</ref> Other one-offs include, the [[Guinness World Records|Guinness World Record]] [[Nissan GT-R in motorsport#Drifting|drift car]],<ref name=":7">{{Cite web|date=2016-04-07|title=A Nissan GT-R has just set a drifting world record|url=https://www.topgear.com/car-news/modified/nissan-gt-r-has-just-set-drifting-world-record|access-date=2021-09-13|website=Top Gear|language=en}}</ref> the GT-R Predzilla that was exclusively built and donated to the [[Nashville Predators|Nashville Predators Foundation]], custom-painted in Preds' official colours and graphics.<ref>{{Cite web|title=Nissan creates 'Predzilla' GT-R for Nashville Predators, proceeds going to charity|url=https://www.motorauthority.com/news/1110851_nissan-creates-predzilla-gt-r-for-nashville-predators-proceeds-going-to-charity|access-date=2021-09-13|website=Motor Authority|date=June 6, 2017 |language=en}}</ref> The Tomica 50th Anniversary GT-R, built to celebrate the 50th anniversary of [[Tomica (toy line)|Tomica]]. Based on the 2017 model year GT-R, it was wrapped up with the iconic red and black "[[Nissan Skyline#RS|Tomica Skyline Turbo Super Silhouette]]" livery, symbolising the relationship between Tomica and Nissan.<ref>{{Cite web|title=Nissan GT-R R35: Tomica 50th Anniversary Specification |url=https://gtr-registry.com/en-r35-tomica-50th-anniversary-specification.php |access-date=2023-09-04 |website=GT-R Registry |language=en}}</ref> A special version of the GT-R Nismo, wrapped in a gold body colour, built in collaboration with [[McDonald's]] in Japan. A toy model was also offered with the “Tomica Happy Set" meal.<ref>{{Cite web|last=Panait|first=Mircea|date=2021-04-17|title=2022 Nissan GT-R NISMO With McDonald's Gold Wrap Is One Cool Promotional Car|url=https://www.autoevolution.com/news/2022-nissan-gt-r-nismo-with-mcdonalds-livery-is-one-cool-promotional-car-159515.html|access-date=2021-08-01|website=autoevolution|language=en}}</ref>
