In 2013, in a joint project between Nissan Russia and LAV Productions, the 2012 model year GT-R set an unofficial national ice speed record for a production car at the [[Lake Baikal]], in southern Siberia, Russia. The record was set by Russian racing driver [[Roman Rusinov]], with a trap speed of 294.8&nbsp;km/h (183&nbsp;mph). This lake is considered as the [[Deepest lake|deepest lake of the world]]. According to Nissan, the record car was in standard specifications with factory standard [[Bridgestone]] tyres.<ref name=":10">{{Cite web |date=2013-04-05 |title=The Record Breaking Nissan GT-R |url=https://usa.nissannews.com/en-US/releases/the-record-breaking-nissan-gt-r |access-date=2022-03-21 |website=Official U.S. Newsroom |language=en-US}}</ref><ref name=":24">{{Cite web |title=Nissan GT-R Sets Unofficial Production Car Ice Speed Record In Russia: Video |url=https://www.motorauthority.com/news/1083318_nissan-gt-r-sets-unofficial-production-car-ice-speed-record-in-russia-video |access-date=2022-03-21 |website=Motor Authority |date=April 2, 2013 |language=en}}</ref>

=== Official Nürburgring ''Nordschleife'' lap times ===
{{See also|List of Nürburgring Nordschleife lap times}}

[[File:Nissan GT-R NISMO N-Attack Package.jpg|thumb|The GT-R Nismo prototype, set the fastest lap time for mass-produced cars at the Nürburgring ''Nordschleife'' in 2013|left]]

Nissan has published numerous lap times for the GT-R around the [[Nürburgring|Nürburgring ''Nordschleife'']]. Due to its demanding nature, the "iconic" racetrack played a pivotal role in the development and served as a performance benchmark for the GT-R.<ref name="NGV" /> Over the years, Nissan conducted numerous time attacks for the car around the ''Nordschleife'', pitting it against [[Porsche]] and [[Chevrolet]] in pursuit of setting the fastest lap time for mass-produced cars, which garnered attention from the automotive media. Both manufacturers, fielded their respective sports cars, the [[Porsche 911|911]] and [[Chevrolet Corvette|Corvette]], and consistently engaged in lap time battles against Nissan with the GT-R.<ref>{{cite web |url=https://www.drive.com.au/news/corvette-zr1-topples-gt-r-at-nurburgring/ |title=Corvette ZR1 topples GT-R at Nürburgring |work=The Drive |date=June 28, 2008 |access-date=2023-10-09}}</ref><ref>{{cite web |url=https://www.motortrend.com/news/did-godzilla-lie-porsche-cries-foul-over-record-nissan-gtr-ring-time-2141/ |title=Did Godzilla Lie? Porsche Cries Foul Over Record Nissan GT-R 'Ring Time 
|work=[[Motor Trend]] |access-date=2023-10-09}}</ref> The lap times were often navigated by former [[List of Formula One drivers|Formula One driver]] and development driver, [[Toshio Suzuki (racing driver)|Toshio Suzuki]], using factory-standard [[Dunlop Tyres|Dunlop]] SP Sport Maxx GT 600 DSST CTT run-flat tyres.<ref name="GT-R Story"/>

Having set a lap time of 7:38.54 minutes in damp conditions before the official launch, Nissan returned to the ''Nordschleife'' with the GT-R in April 2008 and set a lap time of 7:32 minutes.<ref>{{cite web |url=https://www.drive.com.au/news/new-porsche-gt2-clocks-nurburgring-at-732/ |title=New Porsche GT2 clocks Nurburgring at 7:32 |work=The Drive |date=August 9, 2007 |access-date=2023-10-09}}</ref> Observed by ''[[Best Motoring]]'', the GT-R improved its lap time to 7:29.03 minutes in May 2009.<ref name="GT-R Story" /><ref>{{cite web|url=http://www.nissan-global.com/EN/NEWS/2009/_STORY/090514-01-e.html|title=AWARD-WINNING NISSAN GT-R ACHIEVES NEW RECORD LAP TIME AT NÜRBURGRING CIRCUIT|work=Nissan|access-date=June 2, 2009|archive-date=May 18, 2009|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20090518150817/http://www.nissan-global.com/EN/NEWS/2009/_STORY/090514-01-e.html|url-status=dead}}</ref><ref>{{cite AV media |url=https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=mftdOZmNkws |title=R35 GT-R 日産ニュルブルクリンク・タイムアタック!! NURBURGRING ATTACK!!【Best MOTORing】2008 |date=April 17, 2016 |access-date=September 17, 2023 |via=YouTube}}{{cbignore}}</ref> Porsche accused Nissan of overstating the performance of the car, claimed they conducted a test of a customer-spec GT-R and recorded a slower lap time of 7:54 minutes, apparently implying that the car was not as fast around the track as it was claimed.<ref name="PorscheAccusesNissan22">{{cite web|url=http://carsguide.news.com.au/site/motoring-news/story/porsche_accuses_nissan_of_cheating_at_nurburgring/|title=Porsche accuses Nissan of cheating at Nürburgring|last=Gover|first=Paul|date=September 30, 2008|work=Carsguide.com.au|access-date=September 30, 2008}}</ref><ref>{{cite web|url=http://www.autocar.co.uk/News/NewsArticle.aspx?AR=235197|title=Autocar – Porsche says Nissan cheating|publisher=Autocar.co.uk|access-date=October 27, 2008}}</ref> Nissan added the car was in standard specifications, equipped with factory standard tyres and implied that Porsche's driver was not as talented as theirs.<ref name="NissanRefutes22">{{cite web|url=http://www.autoblog.com/2008/10/09/nissan-to-porsche-put-the-gt-r-down-before-you-hurt-yourself/|title=Nissan defends GT-R 'Ring time|last=Roth|first=Dan|date=October 9, 2008|work=[[Autoblog.com|Autoblog]]|access-date=October 3, 2008}}</ref> In the following year, the GT-R with performance upgrades to the 2010 model year, improved its lap time to 7:26.70 minutes.<ref>{{cite AV media |url=https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=alFGVWR0FPw |title=R35 GT-R 日産ニュルブルクリンク・タイムアタック!! NURBURGRING ATTACK!!【Best MOTORing】2009 |date=April 17, 2016 |access-date=September 17, 2023 |via=YouTube}}{{cbignore}}</ref>

In September 2010, Nissan returned to the ''Nordschleife'' with the facelifted GT-R, and set a lap time of 7:24.22 minutes in its first attempt in damp conditions. Due to poor track conditions, the car could not further improve its lap time and settled down with the latter lap time.<ref>{{cite AV media |url=https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=hSq4Xx5Iuls |title=GT-R 2011モデル 日産自動車 開発テスト 密着レポート【Best MOTORing】2010 |date=April 14, 2018 |access-date=September 17, 2023 |via=YouTube}}{{cbignore}}</ref><ref name="AutoGuide-2011-03-2422">{{cite web|url=http://www.autoguide.com/auto-news/2011/03/2012-nissan-gt-r-724-22-nurburgring-lap-time-video.html|title=2012 Nissan GT-R 7:24.22 Nurburgring Lap Time Video|last=Wood|first=Colum|date=March 24, 2011|work=AutoGuide|location=Canada|access-date=April 12, 2019}}</ref> According to Nissan, the GT-R improved its ''Nordschleife'' lap time again in October 2012 to 7:19.1 minutes, by due to the 2013 model year improvements.<ref>{{cite web |url=https://www.motortrend.com/news/video-find-2012-chevrolet-corvette-zr1-cuts-six-seconds-nurburgring-lap-time-85635/ |title=2012 Corvette ZR1 Blisters the 'Ring in 7:19.4 Seconds |work=[[Motor Trend]] |access-date=2023-10-09}}</ref> Nissan claimed that it lost half a second due to traffic, making a potential lap time of 7:18.6 minutes possible, which would equal the limited-production 911 GT2 RS.<ref>{{cite AV media |url=https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=b-1mSAKbKFE |title=日産GT-R 2012年モデル ニュルブルクリンク開発テスト【Best MOTORing】 |date=June 23, 2016 |access-date=September 17, 2023 |via=YouTube}}{{cbignore}}</ref><ref name="CarAdvice201222">{{cite news|last=Crawford|first=Anthony|url=http://www.caradvice.com.au/199112/2013-nissan-gt-r-sets-ninth-quickest-nurburgring-lap-time-in-history/|title=2013 Nissan GT-R sets ninth-quickest Nurburgring lap time in history|date=November 5, 2012|work=CarAdvice|access-date=October 4, 2014|location=Australia}}</ref>

At the end of September 2013, testing was finalized for the GT-R Nismo and the development team was aiming to set a lap time under 7:10 minutes.<ref name="GNDV">{{Citation |title=NISSAN GT-R NISMO Development Story (REVISED) | date=November 21, 2013 |url=https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=YDXoFK_kGJQ |archive-url=https://ghostarchive.org/varchive/youtube/20211215/YDXoFK_kGJQ |language=en |access-date=2020-03-22 |archive-date=2021-12-15 |url-status=live}}{{cbignore}}</ref> In his second attempt, [[Nismo]] racing driver [[Michael Krumm]] recorded a lap time of 7:08.679 minutes and achieved a peak speed of {{cvt|310|km/h|mph|0}} on the Dottinger Hohe uphill straight.<ref>{{Citation |last=日産自動車株式会社 |title=Michael Krumm Attacks Nürburgring in a Nissan GT-R NISMO |date=November 19, 2013 |url=https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=sNAT_c3CLHw |archive-url=https://ghostarchive.org/varchive/youtube/20211215/sNAT_c3CLHw |access-date=April 4, 2019 |archive-date=2021-12-15 |url-status=live}}{{cbignore}}</ref> Nissan claimed it was the lap record for mass-produced cars around the track, and confirmed the record car used was equipped with post-production track options, available to customers through the N-Attack Package.<ref name="Ring Record">{{Cite press release |date=2013-11-19|title=Nissan GT-R Nismo world's fastest volume production car around the "green hell"|url=https://europe.nissannews.com/en-GB/releases/nissan-gt-r-nismo-world-s-fastest-volume-production-car-around-the-green-hell|access-date=2020-06-29|publisher=Nissan |location=Europe}}</ref> The optional track-only bonnet gurney strip was also featured in the record-setting car.<ref>{{Cite web |url=https://www.topgear.com/car-news/modified/nissan-gt-r-50-how-build-ultimate-nissan-gt-r |title=Nissan GT-R at 50: how to build the ultimate Nissan GT-R |access-date=2023-11-10 |website=topgear.com |date=April 18, 2019 |language=en}}</ref>

=== Independent Nürburgring ''Nordschleife'' lap times ===
The car has set independent ''Nordschleife'' lap times in tests conducted by automotive publications, navigated by journalist drivers. In a test conducted by ''[[Drivers Republic]]'', the GT-R and 911 GT2 set lap times of 7:56 minutes and 7:49 minutes respectively in partially damp conditions. The publication claimed the GT2 could achieve the factory lap time of 7:32 minutes, but not the GT-R going faster than 7:41 minutes in spite of the 7:29 minutes of factory claim, however the test car was equipped with the less stickier, Bridgestone summer tyres and [[stability control]].<ref name="DRtest">{{cite web |url=http://magazines.drivers-republic.com/driversrepublic/thetruth030/ |title=The Truth |access-date=November 27, 2008 |last=Harris |first=Chris |date=November 24, 2008 |work=Driver's Republic |page=23 |archive-date=December 3, 2008 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20081203073612/http://magazines.drivers-republic.com/driversrepublic/thetruth030/ |url-status=dead }}</ref><ref>{{cite web|url=https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=HQ2ZmFe80-U |title=Drivers Republic - GT-R v GT2 Nürburgring comparison |website=[[YouTube]] |date=2012-07-17 |access-date=2023-11-07}}</ref>

The German magazine ''[[sport auto (Germany)|Sport Auto]]'' recorded a lap time of 7:50 minutes in a GT-R supplied by Nissan during an initial short test in 2007, in partially damp conditions.<ref>{{cite web |url=http://www.sportauto-online.de/test_U_technik/fahrberichte/hxcms_article_508540_14469.hbs |title=Nissan GT-R: Ost-Erweiterung |access-date=October 2, 2008 |work=sportauto |language=de}}</ref> In 2009, in a full "Supertest", ''Sport Auto'' recorded a lap time of 7:38 minutes, driven by [[Horst von Saurma]].<ref name="SAringtime">{{cite web |url=http://www.sportauto-online.de/supertest/nissan-gt-r-objektive-nordschleifen-rundezeit-des-486-ps-japaners-gtr-1347840.html |title=Objektive Nordschleifen-Rundezeit des Japaners |access-date=July 16, 2009 |work=sportauto |language=de |archive-date=July 18, 2009 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20090718093414/http://www.sportauto-online.de/supertest/nissan-gt-r-objektive-nordschleifen-rundezeit-des-486-ps-japaners-gtr-1347840.html |url-status=dead }}</ref> It was also identical to a lap time of Corvette ZR1, recorded later by the same publication.<ref>{{cite web|url=http://www.sportauto-online.de/supertest/die-staerkste-corvette-zr1-im-supertest-auf-der-nordschleife-1415542.html |title=Corvette ZR1 im Supertest auf der Nordschleife: Was kann die stärkste Corvette aller Zeiten? &#124; Sportauto |publisher=Sportauto-online.de |access-date=December 19, 2009}}</ref> In a test with the 2011 model year GT-R, they recorded a lap time of 7:34 minutes, again driven by Saurma it was only 10 seconds slower than the official claim.<ref>{{cite web |first=Horst |last=von Saurma |url=http://www.sportauto-online.de/einzeltests/nissan-gt-r-2011-im-nordschleifen-test-mit-rundenzeit-3059911.html |title=Nissan GT-R 2011 im ersten Nordschleifen-Test – SPORT AUTO |publisher=Sportauto-online.de |date=April 22, 2011 |access-date=November 20, 2011 |archive-date=November 13, 2011 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20111113000059/http://www.sportauto-online.de/einzeltests/nissan-gt-r-2011-im-nordschleifen-test-mit-rundenzeit-3059911.html |url-status=dead }}</ref>

