In addition to these accolades, the GT-R has also set [[Guinness World Records]] for the fastest accelerating four-seater production car, ice speed record for a production car, and fastest drift speed record.<ref name=":8" /><ref name=":24" /><ref name=":7"/> In 2010, it was named as having one of the best resale values of any sports car by ''[[Yahoo!]]''.<ref>{{Cite web |title=Sports cars with best resale value{{!}} Yahoo Autos |url=http://autos.yahoo.com/articles/autos_content_landing_pages/1487/sports-cars-with-the-best-resale-value/ |access-date=2023-02-05 |website=Autoblog |language=en |archive-date=September 30, 2010 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20100930033631/http://autos.yahoo.com/articles/autos_content_landing_pages/1487/sports-cars-with-the-best-resale-value/ |url-status=dead }}</ref> ''Top Gear'', ''[[Auto Express]]'' and ''Car Connection'' entitled the GT-R as one of the best performance cars in 2015.<ref>{{Cite web |date=2015-12-17 |title=Top Gear's top five sports cars |url=https://www.topgear.com/car-news/best-2015/top-gears-top-five-sports-cars |access-date=2023-02-05 |website=Top Gear |language=en}}</ref><ref>{{Cite web |title=Nissan GT-R - best sports cars |url=https://www.autoexpress.co.uk/nissan/gt-r/96404/nissan-gt-r-best-sports-cars |access-date=2023-02-05 |website=Auto Express |language=en}}</ref><ref>{{Cite web |last=Director |first=Martin Padgett Editorial |title=The Best Performance Cars Of 2015 |url=https://www.thecarconnection.com/news/1097645_the-best-performance-cars-of-2015 |access-date=2023-02-05 |website=The Car Connection |language=en}}</ref> ''Car Connection'', again claimed the GT-R as one of the best performance cars in 2019.<ref>{{Cite web |last=Cole |first=Aaron |title=The Car Connection's Best Performing Cars of 2019 |url=https://www.thecarconnection.com/news/1123205_the-car-connections-best-performing-cars-of-2019 |access-date=2023-02-05 |website=The Car Connection |language=en}}</ref> In 2021 and 2022, ''Autocar'' and ''Auto Express'' named it as one of the best hardcore sports cars.<ref>{{Cite web |title=Top 10 best super sports cars 2022 |url=https://www.autocar.co.uk/car-news/best-cars/top-10-best-super-sports-cars |access-date=2023-02-05 |website=Autocar |language=en}}</ref><ref>{{Cite web |title=Top 10 best hardcore sports cars 2022 |url=https://www.autocar.co.uk/car-news/best-cars/top-10-best-hardcore-sports-cars |access-date=2023-02-05 |website=Autocar |language=en}}</ref><ref>{{Cite web |title=Top 10 best sports cars 2022 |url=https://www.autoexpress.co.uk/best-cars-vans/106907/top-10-best-sports-cars-2022 |access-date=2023-02-05 |website=Auto Express |language=en}}</ref> ''Road & Track'' mentioned the GT-R as one of the best daily drivers, while ''[[Evo (magazine)|Evo Magazine]]'' claimed it as one of the best coupes in 2022.<ref>{{Cite web |last=Silvestro |first=Brian |date=2022-04-28 |title=Sports Cars That Make Great Daily Drivers in 2023 |url=https://www.roadandtrack.com/car-culture/g13132454/daily-driver-sports-cars/ |access-date=2023-02-05 |website=Road & Track |language=en-US}}</ref><ref>{{Cite web |title=Best coupes 2022 – our top ten style-led sports cars in classical form |url=https://www.evo.co.uk/coupes/20746/best-coupes-2022-our-top-ten-style-led-sports-cars-in-classical-form |access-date=2023-02-05 |website=evo |language=en}}</ref> ''[[Carwow]]'' named the GT-R as one of the best sports cars of 2023.<ref>{{Cite web |title=10 Best Sports Cars of 2023 |url=https://www.carwow.co.uk/sports-cars |access-date=2023-02-11 |website=www.carwow.co.uk |language=en}}</ref> ''Car and Driver'' listed it as one of the best luxury sports cars of 2024.<ref>{{Cite web |title=Best Luxury Sports Cars of 2024 |url=https://www.caranddriver.com/rankings/best-sports-cars/premium |access-date=2023-09-25 |website=caranddriver.com |language=en}}</ref>

== Motorsport ==
{{main article|Nissan GT-R in motorsport}}

{{See also|Nissan GT-R LM Nismo}}
[[File:Safety Car 2010 Super GT Fuji 400km.jpg|thumb|GT-R safety car in the Super GT series|left]]
The GT-R competed across a wide range of racing disciplines, attaining multiple successes. Notable [[motorsport]] achievements came through from its participation in [[sports car racing]], including championship triumphs in the approvingly competitive [[FIA GT1 World Championship]], [[SRO Motorsports Group#GT World Challenge|GT World Challenge]] and in the [[Super GT]] series. As well as in [[Endurance racing (motorsport)|endurance races]], with consistent top order finishes in the [[Bathurst 12 Hour]], [[Nürburgring 24 Hours]], [[Spa 24 Hours]] among others. The car was used as the official [[safety car]] in numerous motorsport events, such as in the Super GT series, FIA GT1 World Championship,<ref>{{Cite web |title=Nissan is Official Car for the FIA GT1 World Championship |url=https://www.drive.com.au/news/nissan-is-official-car-for-the-fia-gt1-world-championship/ |access-date=2023-09-06 |website=drive.com.au |date=April 14, 2010 |language=en}}</ref> [[British Superbike Championship]],<ref>{{Cite web |title=Nissan Becomes the British Superbike Championship's Official Vehicle Supplier |url=https://www.autoevolution.com/news/nissan-becomes-the-british-superbike-championship-s-official-vehicle-supplier-18469.html |access-date=2023-09-06 |website=autoevolution.com |date=March 25, 2010 |language=en}}</ref> and in the [[Supercars Championship]].<ref>{{Cite web |title=2009 Nissan GT-R To Act As Safety Car For 2009 Australian V8 Supercar Series |url=https://www.drive.com.au/news/2009-nissan-gt-r-to-act-as-safety-car-for-2009-australian-v8-supercar-series/ |access-date=2023-09-06 |website=drive.com.au |date=March 3, 2009 |language=en}}</ref>
{{clear}}

== Legacy ==
Critics agreed the GT-R is among the best Japanese automobiles,<ref>{{Cite web|title=100 Greatest Japanese Cars of All Time|url=https://www.edmunds.com/car-reviews/features/100-greatest-japanese-cars-of-all-time.html|access-date=2025-12-21|website=Edmunds|language=en}}</ref><ref>{{Cite web|title=These are 10 of the best Japanese performance cars
|url=https://www.topgear.com/car-news/top-gear-advice/these-are-10-best-japanese-performance-cars|access-date=2025-12-21|website=Top Gear|language=en}}</ref><ref>{{Cite web|date=2024-04-17|title=The Best Japanese Sports Cars Ever Made
|url=https://www.roadandtrack.com/car-culture/g6248/hottest-japanese-sports-cars-ever/|access-date=2025-12-21|website=Road & Track|language=en}}</ref> with some listing it among the best of the 21st century,<ref>{{Cite web|date=2013-10-04|title=The 50 greatest cars of the past 20 years
|url=https://www.topgear.com/car-news/list/50-greatest-cars-past-20-years|access-date=2025-12-21|website=Top Gear|language=en}}</ref><ref>{{Cite web|date=2025-07-13|title=The 25 Most Memorable Cars of The Last 25 Years
|url=https://www.hagerty.com/media/automotive-history/the-25-most-memorable-cars-of-the-last-25-years/|access-date=2025-12-21|website=Hagerty Media|language=en}}</ref> and of all time.<ref>{{Cite web|date=2015-01-26|title=CAR’s 50 greatest cars revealed
|url=https://www.carmagazine.co.uk/car-news/magazine/cars-50-greatest-cars-revealed-/|access-date=2025-12-21|website=Car Magazine|language=en}}</ref><ref name=LegacyTG>{{Cite web|title=Top Gear mag's greatest cars - supercars
|url=https://www.topgear.com/car-news/supercars/top-gear-mags-greatest-cars-supercars|access-date=2025-12-21|website=Top Gear|language=en}}</ref><ref>{{Cite web|date=2011-10-29|title=The 100 Greatest Cars Of All Time...
|url=https://www.pistonheads.com/news/general-pistonheads/the-100-greatest-cars-of-all-time/24425|access-date=2025-12-21|website=PetrolHeads|language=en}}</ref><ref>{{Cite web|date=2022-06-22|title=This Is Our Definitive List of the 103 Coolest Cars of All Time
|url=https://www.popularmechanics.com/cars/g93/the-100-hottest-cars-of-all-time/|access-date=2025-12-21|website=Popular Mechanics|language=en}}</ref> At the time of its release, featuring advanced technologies such as [[Launch control (automotive)|launch control]] and a [[dual-clutch transmission]]—which were not common among production cars were seen as transformative, and altering the expectations for sports cars.<ref name="LegacyEvo1">{{Cite web|date=2025-12-15|title=Cars that ended production in 2025
|url=https://www.evo.co.uk/best-cars/208382/cars-that-ended-production-in-2025|access-date=2025-12-21|website=Evo|language=en}}</ref><ref name="LegacyR&D">{{Cite web|date=2025-03-24|title=The R35-Gen Nissan GT-R's Story May Be Over, But It Won't Soon Be Forgotten
|url=https://www.roadandtrack.com/news/a64234492/r35-generation-nissan-gt-r-retrospective/|access-date=2025-12-21|website=Road & Track|language=en}}</ref> Following its release, these technologies became increasingly widespread, ''[[Motor Trend]]'' listed the GT-R as it has changed the automotive industry, noting that "it altered the supercar landscape, leaving competitors scratching their heads".<ref>{{Cite web|date=2014-07-14|title=13 Automotive Game-Changers: Cars that Forever Altered the Automotive Industry
|url=https://www.motortrend.com/features/these-cars-and-trucks-changed-the-game|access-date=2025-12-21|website=Motor Trend|language=en}}</ref> Critics noted it has played a critical role in the democratisation of high-performance sports cars,<ref name="LegacyR&D" /><ref name="LegacyEvo1" /><ref>{{Cite web|date=2025-10-18|title=Nissan GT-R R35 Bids a Fond Farewell: The End of a Legend That Redefined Performance
|url=https://luxe.outlookindia.com/tech-auto/auto/nissan-gtr-r35-bids-a-fond-farewell-the-end-of-a-legend-that-redefined-performance|access-date=2025-12-21|website=Outlook Luxe|language=en}}</ref> with influence extending to modern manufacturers' priority on [[Nürburgring]] lap times.<ref name="LegacyC&D">{{Cite web|date=2025-08-27|title=Nissan GT-R Production Has Ended, and This Is the Final R35
|url=https://www.caranddriver.com/news/a65903913/nissan-gt-r-production-ends/|access-date=2025-12-21|website=Car and Driver|language=en}}</ref> ''The Drive'' credited the GT-R as an inspiration for unconventional vehicles, such as [[Sports sedan|sport sedans]] and [[SUV]]s to incorporate advanced technologies, and achieve sports car-like performance figures.<ref>{{Cite web|date=2025-12-06|title=The Nissan R35 GT-R Turns 15 Today. Here’s a Look Back at Our Supercar Teenager
|url=https://www.thedrive.com/news/the-nissan-r35-gt-r-turns-15-today-heres-a-look-back-at-our-supercar-teenager|access-date=2025-12-21|website=The Drive|language=en}}</ref>

The GT-R has been regarded as a benchmark for sports car performance.<ref name="LegacyTopGear">{{Cite web|date=2025-07-04|title=Sayonara, Godzilla: one last ride through Tokyo in the R35 Nissan GT-R
|url=https://www.topgear.com/car-news/big-reads/sayonara-godzilla-one-last-ride-through-tokyo-r35-nissan-gt-r|access-date=2025-12-21|website=Top Gear|language=en}}</ref><ref name="LegacyCarEx">{{Cite web|date=2025-08-31|title=R35 Nissan GT-R: Mission accomplished
|url=https://www.carexpert.com.au/car-news/r35-nissan-gt-r-mission-accomplished|access-date=2025-12-21|website=Car Expert|language=en}}</ref><ref name="LegacyEvo2">{{Cite web|date=2025-10-15|title=The R35 Nissan GT-R is dead after 18 years, and it bows out as a legend
|url=https://www.evo.co.uk/nissan/gt-r/208103/the-nissan-gt-r-is-finally-dead-after-18-years|access-date=2025-12-21|website=Evo|language=en}}</ref> ''[[Road & Track]]'' claimed achieving or surpassing the performance of more expensive sports cars was "unheard of" at the time of its release.<ref name=LegacyR&D /> The GT-R has a wide and active aftermarket tuning community, with significant influence among automotive enthusiasts.<ref name=LegacyR&D /><ref name="LegacyTopGear" /> Whilst it was initially criticised for assisted driving experiences at the time of release, it was later praised for "analogue" feel amid the increasing number of sports cars featuring digital driving experiences.<ref>{{Cite web|date=2016-11-04|title=The 2017 Nissan GT-R Nismo Is Suddenly an Analog Sports Car
|url=https://www.roadandtrack.com/car-culture/a31434/the-2017-nissan-gt-r-nismo-is-suddenly-an-analog-sports-car/|access-date=2025-12-21|website=Road & Track|language=en}}</ref><ref>{{Cite web|date=2025-09-29|title=Nissan GT-R (R35, 2009 - 2025) review – the Porsche 911 Turbo’s greatest rival
|url=https://www.evo.co.uk/nissan/gt-r|access-date=2025-12-21|website=Evo|language=en}}</ref> Including its later years, critics found the GT-R had remained comparable to newer competition in terms of performance, due to consistent updates over its 18-year production span.<ref name="LegacyC&D" /><ref name="LegacyCarEx" /><ref name="LegacyEvo2" /><ref name="LegacyTopGear" />

